      ],
      "reason": "A leaf seat's completed silent end now wakes the seat itself for the first two ends of a run and gives its parent the counted line only from the third, so the guarantee that a silent end wakes the waiting agent narrows for Workers, Reviewers and Curators; the same revision corrects the return's realization so the recogniser reads every row shape that shows the recipient. The Reviewer's separate producer list was read against the same freeze: its nine clause entries — eight behavioural clauses and the code-proof clause MIK-R183-v5-R9-CODE, which states that the proof uses exact captures, consequential effects and source-bound before/after controls — restate the obligations this record already carries, its F06/F07 dispositions match the conditions and proofs below, and its lineage decision, postlanding measurement and ruled-intent entry add no record change. Two proof facets of this invariant are not in this change: PRF-QSEPFH and PRF-M65N8C are owned by leaf 260928-MIK-L172, their test bodies were measured unchanged across this leaf, and the writer offers no facet revision — so they are named here as owned elsewhere and blocked by the writer, not silently absent. Evidence (MIK-R183@v5/INV-1ZKP4R): Worker A6 producer list (eight v5 clause entries, their statements carried there) sha256 58f2d2da8f5153f629dc5551076066791089a444496eefad1c75184ec9a506df; Reviewer A6 producer list (fourteen entries: nine clause entries — the eight behavioural clauses plus MIK-R183-v5-R9-CODE, the code-proof clause — F06/F07 fixed, the lineage decision, the postlanding measurement and the ruled-intent entry) sha256 d990aa8468c04e2edb462cde806ff6c4ba49cf8c3093acb7bc4ef9310089c7f7; A6 report c98914512d3b39e1025102a1726a185ccacc123c847214d2ea8c9cbe662ae0f7; reviewer CODE PASS verdict, tree faf66c3edc234bd23b7a16780218611586556fc9, effects 46/46; successor base-move freeze A6-base-move-48a754e7.md sha256 5af1f5f6c0ccc57df7e18aa21711fc00eb78b7e36d02230f15ae742e814a9621, tree 5472cbf6eda1b323571dc69b9081f9b6a2b6a2a5 on code base 48a754e7 and memory base 83acf829 under the Manager/Architect pure-sync ruling; then the L104 base move to code 47f69f11afb982e318006209036aed22f1792976 and memory 804d7d813a1e1afac1043163825235e08d060f53 (contract sync 12:30:54Z), where the candidate trees are dffdb8e4a3fac69d18aeb442217163ba2dec7382 for code and d460bfcd07ede8313e513d9c2af7065f18b61a05 for memory. The 153408-byte change is byte-identical throughout. This memory candidate is re-derived on the current pair and replaces the earlier candidates whose bases moved; it does not replace a candidate that was wrong.",
